* fetch: a jump to code that is in no instruction buffer.
* NOSTEP
* The X-MP takes 19 clock periods for it (CSM-0111000 section 5).  The core
* reads half a buffer, 16 words one behind the other, before the first
* instruction there can issue, so it takes more however fast memory is: 23
* with a memory that answers in the next clock.  The test fails if the
* first instruction issues sooner than the X-MP's 19, or later than 400.
* The jump is made when the block it is in has been read whole, which the
* loop before it waits for.
         INCLUDE "rt_direct.cal"
         TBEGIN
         A1      D'60
WAIT     A1      A1-1
         A0      A1
         JAN     WAIT
         S6      RT
         J       FAR
         ORG     4000
FAR      S7      RT
         S7      S7-S6                   ; clock periods, and one for the first reading
         S1      D'20
         S0      S7-S1
         JSP     OK1
         TFAIL   2                       ; sooner than the X-MP
OK1      S1      D'400
         S0      S1-S7
         JSP     OK2
         TFAIL   3                       ; much too late
OK2      TPASS
         TEND
         END
